<body>

  {% include "nav.njk" %}

  <main>

    <!-- PAGE HERO -->
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Mental Health Resources</span>
        <h1>Resources to help you understand what you're carrying.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Here are some resources that might help. Each guide is written in plain language. No jargon, no judgment. Just honest information about what's going on and what can actually help.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- RESOURCE CARDS -->
    <section class="section resources-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Featured</span>
          <h2>A workbook you can start on your own.</h2>
        </div>

        <article class="feature-workbook reveal">
          <div class="feature-workbook-art">
            <img src="/images/carry-the-weight-cover.webp" width="920" height="920" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
                 alt="Cover of Carry the Weight, Not the Damage, a men's mental health workbook">
          </div>
          <div class="feature-workbook-body">
            <span class="feature-workbook-tag">Workbook for Men</span>
            <h3>Carry the Weight,<br>Not the Damage</h3>
            <p>Twenty-seven pages of the same practical tools used in a therapy room, written in plain
            language for the man who looks fine on paper and knows something underneath isn't. Work
            through it at your own pace, on your own time.</p>
            <div class="feature-workbook-meta">
              <span>Anger that arrives too fast</span>
              <span>Running on empty</span>
              <span>A mind that won't shut off</span>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-workbook-buy">
              <div class="feature-workbook-price">$14<small>27 pages · instant PDF</small></div>
              <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/carry-the-weight">See the Workbook</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:72px;">
          <span class="eyebrow">Free Guides</span>
          <h2>Start with what feels most relevant.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-card reveal">
            <span class="resource-card-category">Mental Health</span>
            <h3>Making Sense of Depression</h3>
            <p>A clear look at what depression is, how it affects your mind and body, why it happens, and what actually helps, without the stigma or oversimplification.</p>
            <a class="resource-card-link" href="/depression">Read This Guide &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="resource-card reveal">
            <span class="resource-card-category">Mental Health</span>
            <h3>Why Anxiety Happens</h3>
            <p>What anxiety actually is, why your brain does it, how it shows up in your body and thoughts, and what helps beyond just pushing through.</p>
            <a class="resource-card-link" href="/anxiety">Read This Guide &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="resource-card reveal">
            <span class="resource-card-category">Mental Health</span>
            <h3>How Trauma Works</h3>
            <p>Trauma isn't defined by the size of what happened. It's defined by the impact. A plain-language guide to what trauma is, how it affects the nervous system, and what healing looks like.</p>
            <a class="resource-card-link" href="/trauma">Read This Guide &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="resource-card reveal">
            <span class="resource-card-category">Mental Health</span>
            <h3>Why Relationship Patterns Repeat</h3>
            <p>The same argument with a different person, the same distance arriving at the same point. Where those patterns are learned, why insight alone does not stop them, and what actually interrupts them.</p>
            <a class="resource-card-link" href="/relationships">Read This Guide &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="resource-card reveal">
            <span class="resource-card-category">Mental Health</span>
            <h3>Understanding Burnout</h3>
            <p>What burnout actually is, how it differs from depression, why rest stops working, and what recovery genuinely requires beyond a long weekend.</p>
            <a class="resource-card-link" href="/burnout">Read This Guide &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="resource-card reveal">
            <span class="resource-card-category">Veterans &amp; Service</span>
            <h3>Life After Service</h3>
            <p>Why the training does not switch off when the service ends. How hypervigilance, transition, and moral injury actually work, and what can be retrained.</p>
            <a class="resource-card-link" href="/veterans">Read This Guide &rarr;</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FINAL CTA -->
    <section class="final-cta">
      <div class="container reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Take the Next Step</span>
        <h2>Ready to talk to someone?</h2>
        <p>Reading about it is a start. Therapy takes it further.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/intake">Book a Free 15-Minute Call</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  {% include "footer.njk" %}

  <script>
    const navToggle = document.getElementById('nav-toggle');
    const navLinks = document.getElementById('nav-links');
    navToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const open = navLinks.classList.toggle('open');
      navToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
    });
    navLinks.querySelectorAll('a').forEach(link => link.addEventListener('click', () => {
      navLinks.classList.remove('open');
      navToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    }));
    document.getElementById('year').textContent = new Date().getFullYear();

    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
      entries.forEach(entry => { if (entry.isIntersecting) entry.target.classList.add('visible'); });
    }, { threshold: .12 });
    document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
  </script>
